+| Item | Status | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| R16-GPT-01 | FIXED | [integrity.mjs:66](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:66) resolves opacity filters; [line 112](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:112) inspects the full composed chain; [line 240](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:240) blocks unresolved effects. [panel-r16.test.mjs:44](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tests/panel-r16.test.mjs:44) asserts filter fades, blur, ancestor brightness, blending above an opaque child, masks and identity controls. Stored before/after logs show assertion failures against the old code and passes afterward. |
+| R16-GPT-02 | PARTIAL | Native text and control records were added at [integrity.mjs:84](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:84) and [line 147](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:147). [panel-r16.test.mjs:72](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tests/panel-r16.test.mjs:72) catches the original faded-submit and scripted-label cases, but misses displayed values masked by accessible names and placeholder opacity. Findings below. |
+| R16-GPT-03 | FIXED | [handoff-contract.mjs:111](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/handoff-contract.mjs:111) requires existing pages and default locale renderings; [line 161](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/handoff-contract.mjs:161) requires all-language manual coverage. [pre-handoff-check.mjs:229](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/pre-handoff-check.mjs:229) renders each screen/locale. [Contract assertions:146](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tests/handoff-contract.test.mjs:146) test missing pages, renderings and Arabic manual records; [fixture:169](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tests/local-fixture.mjs:169) tests runner coverage. |
+| R16-GPT-04 | FIXED | [FANNAN-PLAN.md:77](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/FANNAN-PLAN.md:77) supplies the canonical-specification rule. [handoff-contract.mjs:144](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/handoff-contract.mjs:144) validates definitions/references and repeated specifications; [line 191](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/handoff-contract.mjs:191) requires the critic comparison. [quality-checks.json:48](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/runtime/quality-checks.json:48) requires `component-consistency`. [Contract assertions:160](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tests/handoff-contract.test.mjs:160) test divergent specifications, unknown components/variants, missing comparison coverage and missing manual records. |
+
+Evidence scope: document tests executed PASS. The actual contract assertions executed PASS with an in-memory filesystem and expected FAIL against `5fe9101`. Browser/full-gate results are **reported-only** from stored logs; they were not rerun because those tests create files.
+
+| ID | Part | Severity | file:line | Evidence | Exact fix |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| R17-GPT-01 | A | P2 | [integrity.mjs:151](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:151), [158](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:158) | **R16-GPT-02 remains partial; N12/N13/N14.** `nameOf` prioritizes `aria-label`, while `shownValue` excludes `'submit', 'reset', 'button'`. For `<input type="submit" aria-label="Continue" value="">` whose script supplies `.value="Continue"`, the displayed label disappears without JavaScript but both content records remain `["input:submit","Continue",""]`. Executed in-memory repro: contrast coverage decreases **2→1**, yet integrity returns **PASS**. Browser rendering **UNVERIFIED**. | Record a button-type input’s displayed value independently of its accessible name. Compare both across renderings. Add this combined ARIA-label/value regression with an unrelated heading, requiring a content mismatch and `pass:false`. |
+| R17-GPT-02 | A | P2 | [integrity.mjs:104](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:104), [124](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/integrity.mjs:124) | **R16-GPT-02 remains partial; N12.** Placeholder measurement reads only `getComputedStyle(el, '::placeholder').color`; its opacity and typography are omitted. Ordinary `input::placeholder {color:#000;opacity:.05}` therefore measures as opaque black. Executed in-memory repro with placeholder opacity **1 versus .05** returns identical results: checked **2**, failures **0**, unknown **0**. Browser rendering **UNVERIFIED**. | Composite the placeholder’s own opacity and use its computed font size/weight for the contrast threshold. Unsupported native painting must remain incomplete. Add a JavaScript-restored placeholder-opacity regression and a readable control. |
+| R17-GPT-03 | A | P2 | [pre-handoff-check.mjs:105](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/pre-handoff-check.mjs:105), [116](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/pre-handoff-check.mjs:116); [design-probe.mjs:77](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/tools/design-probe.mjs:77) | Copy validation walks text nodes and compares `norm(matches[0].textContent)`. Design copy screening reads `document.body.innerText`. Native values/placeholders are absent from both. Executed in-memory repro: an **unlisted** `<input placeholder="[placeholder]">` produces `copyProbe: {errors:[],pass:true}`. Conversely, annotating a native value directly cannot match its nonempty deck text through `textContent`. Full browser gate **UNVERIFIED**. | Extract authored native labels, placeholders and displayed option labels for copy-deck matching and filler/placeholder screening. Bind each string to its approved locale slot; distinguish fixture/user-entered data explicitly. Add positive sourced-native-copy tests and negative unlisted, mismatched, filler and placeholder tests. |
+
+**PANEL ANSWER:** **Keep as is.** Token-pair contrast alone cannot establish the result of spatial filters or blending with the actual backdrop. A named approver does not resolve that measurement gap under the stated fail-closed threat model.
+
+Add after [design-quality.md:13](/workspace/panel-r17/fannan/release/references/design-quality.md:13), mirrored in the handoff contract:
+
+> Unresolved compositing on displayed text in either rendering blocks handoff as INCOMPLETE. Token contrast proofs and `jsOffDifferences` cannot waive it. Retaining the effect requires a reviewed measurement implementation that resolves its actual composition for every applicable rendering. Backdrop-filter remains a hard FAIL.
+
+Severity of leaving the current restriction unchanged: **ENH**.
+
+VERDICT: 3 ISSUES (A: 3 P0-P2, B: 0 P0-P2)
