Existing browser before/after results are **reported-only**, supported by the stored logs and inspected assertions. New in-memory reproductions below were **executed** without filesystem writes. Browser/full-checker reproduction of the new examples is **UNVERIFIED**.

| ID | Part | Severity | file:line | Evidence | Exact fix |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| R18-GPT-01 | A | P2 | `release/tools/pre-handoff-check.mjs:118`, `:129`, `:132` | **False positive:** `native()` collects value and `aria-label`, then `native(e).join(' ')` must equal one deck string. Executed extracted `copyProbe`: `<input type="submit" value="Send" aria-label="Send" data-copy-slot="send">` with approved text `Send` fails because the comparison becomes `Send Send`. `<button aria-label="Read more about pricing">Read more</button>` also fails when its visible text is correctly approved. Exact visible-text equality and requiring the expanded name inside that same string are incompatible. | Match displayed text and accessible-name text independently to explicitly identified approved copy fields/slots. Deduplicate identical strings where appropriate; do not require concatenated duplicate copy. Preserve integrity’s separate name/value records. Add positive tests for identical names/values and separately approved expanded names, plus a real mismatch negative. |
| R18-GPT-02 | A | P2 | `release/tools/design-probe.mjs:83`; `release/tools/pre-handoff-check.mjs:118`; `release/tools/integrity.mjs:166` | Native option extraction consistently uses `o.text`, although an option’s displayed label can come from its `label` attribute. `<option label="[placeholder]">Basic plan</option>` therefore supplies `Basic plan` to the new explicit screening/deck paths. A script changing only that label also leaves the recorded selected-option text unchanged. Existing tests use text-node labels only. | Extract the effective option label (`option.label`, with its text fallback) consistently for screening, deck matching and content equivalence. Include authored optgroup labels and both displayed datalist strings where applicable. Add regressions for `label="[placeholder]"`, filler in a label, an approved clean label, and a label changed only by JavaScript. |
| R18-GPT-03 | A | P2 | `release/tools/visibility.mjs:107` | The eligibility condition requires **`el.checkVisibility() && el.getClientRects().length`** before reading text ranges. A `display: contents` element has rendered text but no principal box and is skipped. Executed DOM-model reproduction returns no target IDs for its direct text. A white preloader covering only that text consequently has nothing for this backstop to assess. This repeats the visibility-selection problem addressed by **N02**, now in the new scanner. | Determine text eligibility from rendered text-node ranges and composed ancestor visibility, including `display: contents`; do not require an element box first. Add a positive ordinary-wrapper regression and a negative preloader-over-wrapper regression in both renderings. |
| R18-GPT-04 | A | P2 | `release/tools/visibility.mjs:95`, `:100`, `:136`; `release/tools/integrity.mjs:261` | **False positive:** a sibling layer counts as covering text whenever its background alpha is **`> 0.02`**; covering more than half the sample points is an unconditional failure. Executed reproduction with `background:rgba(255,255,255,.03)` reports `covered:3`, `points:3`, `obscured:true`. A harmless 3% white veil over black text on white retains roughly 20:1 contrast but fails regardless of the pixel result. | Distinguish translucent composition from opaque occlusion. Resolve actual rendered text visibility/contrast before declaring translucent coverage a failure; remain INCOMPLETE when it cannot be resolved. Add paired positive translucent-veil and negative opaque-cover tests, including gradients. |
| R18-GPT-05 | A | P2 | `release/tools/visibility.mjs:43`, `:88`, `:126` | **False positive:** only the document is scrolled; `clipOf()` treats inner scrollports as clipping boundaries. A normal desktop application with a fixed shell and an independently scrolling main panel marks its reachable lower paragraphs **“clipped to nothing.”** Executed geometry reproduction confirms that status. The same problem affects a keyboard-accessible wide table with approved reflow evidence; the scanner never scrolls horizontally. This conflicts with the reachable-scroller handling associated with **N15**. | Traverse reachable positions of nested vertical and horizontal scrollports, preserving/restoring their positions and combining measured coverage by stable target identity. Keep unreachable clipping blocking. Add healthy fixed-shell/inner-scroll and approved wide-table regressions, with inaccessible equivalents that still fail. |
| R18-GPT-06 | A | P2 | `release/tools/visibility.mjs:39`, `:209`, `:225` | **False positive:** **`maxBands:60`** stops the scan before the end of otherwise valid long pages. Executed scanner reproduction for a 36,000px document at 900px viewport height stops at `y=26550`, then labels its reachable footer **“never wholly inside one viewport.”** This is a scan-budget failure presented as unmeasurable design content. | Complete coverage of finite pages using target-directed sampling or resumable bounded scan batches. Do not declare a complete result until every required target has been visited. Add a healthy page exceeding 60 bands and a hidden-text negative beyond that boundary. |
| R18-GPT-07 | A | P2 | `release/tools/visibility.mjs:175`, `:183`, `:185`, `:204`; `:100` | Pixels from all line boxes are pooled, and the **90th-percentile remaining ink contrast** determines the whole element’s result. Executed pixel/scanner/integrity reproduction: three painted lines with JavaScript versus only the first line without it both produce `textMeasured:1`, `textUnreadable:0`; integrity returns **PASS**. A three-line reveal left at `clip-path:inset(0 0 66% 0)` is a concrete honest-mistake case. A pointer-transparent fade hiding the lower lines has the same weakness. Missing lines contribute background pixels rather than failing ink coverage; hit testing also accepts an ancestor when the clipped target is absent. | Verify painted coverage and contrast per text run/line, retaining those identities across renderings. Missing required lines must fail or remain INCOMPLETE rather than borrowing another line’s ink score. Add partial clip-path and `pointer-events:none` fade regressions that preserve one readable line while hiding the others, plus fully readable positives. |

VERDICT: 7 ISSUES (A: 7 P0-P2, B: 0 P0-P2)
